    {
      "file": "web/app/src/features/applications/components/logs/workspace/useApplicationLogsController.tsx",
      "rule": "react-doctor/exhaustive-deps",
      "sourceSha256": "96fed7cbb62571e662c6ef0b039e2d23996bdcd6d8a1ad256e56b43d5e7f73b8",
      "reason": "initialSearchState = useMemo(readApplicationLogsSearchState, []) intentionally captures the initial URL once, before seeding editable detail/trace state. The imported module helper has no React closure dependencies. Subsequent browser location changes are handled by the separately registered popstate listener using the current application owner, not by remounting initial state. Reassessed at the migrated owner: The migrated hook still owns browser popstate and viewport listeners, application-scoped pagination, durable archive upload/download and restoration; ApplicationLogsWorkspace only consumes the returned controls. readApplicationLogsSearchState is a module-scope browser snapshot helper read once on mount; popstate has a separate subscribed reconciliation path. Sequential archive exports preserve per-application progress and download order. Loading is an asynchronous live region, not form output.",
      "evidence": [{"file":"web/app/src/features/applications/components/logs/workspace/useApplicationLogsController.tsx","sha256":"96fed7cbb62571e662c6ef0b039e2d23996bdcd6d8a1ad256e56b43d5e7f73b8"}, {"file":"web/app/src/features/applications/components/logs/workspace/application-logs-controls.ts","sha256":"eafa40879f90f1c88b577887875dcaba21e1556bab113e443ddec226edd9ba74"}, {"file":"web/app/src/features/applications/_tests/application-logs-page/floating-windows/floating-windows-window-navigation.test.tsx","sha256":"aaeafe9fc50cfb2d94706102a134950829e214b33840a526cc5c1a6494b8e2e3"}]
