      "reason": "The effect applies one external lifecycle transition to independent local state; it does not create a self-triggering update cycle. ApplicationLogsWorkspace owns server filters, table selection, URL/popstate synchronization and three independent overlays. Existing extracted overlay helpers own detail/trace/timeline rendering. Viewport resize clamps existing rectangles; application changes reset pagination; popstate applies external browser state. These have external event/resource owners. Reassessed at the migrated owner: The migrated hook still owns browser popstate and viewport listeners, application-scoped pagination, durable archive upload/download and restoration; ApplicationLogsWorkspace only consumes the returned controls. readApplicationLogsSearchState is a module-scope browser snapshot helper read once on mount; popstate has a separate subscribed reconciliation path. Sequential archive exports preserve per-application progress and download order. Loading is an asynchronous live region, not form output.",
